# ADR-0001: Use a modular monolith for the billing application

## Context

What forces the decision: the requirement, the constraint, the legacy behaviour, the options that are open. Two or three short paragraphs; cite the documents (`../blueprint.md`, a requirement id) instead of repeating them.

## Decision

What was decided, in one or two sentences a builder can act on: "The billing application is built as one deployable with a module per business area; modules call each other only through their public interface."

## Consequences

| Becomes easier | Becomes harder |
| --- | --- |
| One deployment, one database transaction across modules | A module cannot be scaled or released on its own |

Follow-up work, risks and what to verify afterwards.

## Alternatives considered

| Option | Why not |
| --- | --- |
| Services per business area | Too many deployables for the team size; no need to scale areas separately |
